ce where users can inspect graph metrics, hover and select nodes without jitter or movement, and navigate directly to verified government source documentation for any selected entity.\n- **`{correct required outputs}`:**\n  1. Top toolbar rendered without the \"Freeze Physics\" / \"Unfreeze\" button.\n  2. Collapsible Blueprint HUD accordion toggling between collapsed and expanded states.\n  3. Stationary canvas nodes during cursor hover and click interactions.\n  4. Dynamic, live government links for `CoveragePolicy`, `PublicLaw`, `Bill`, `Regulation`, `StatutorySection`, `ChangeRequest`, `Jurisdiction`, `HCPCSCode`, `ICD10Code`, and `LobbyingFiling`.\n\n### 1.2 Articulation of Desired Functionality\nThe specification defines four discrete frontend visualizer improvements:\n1. **Toolbar Cleanup \u0026 Autonomous Settle:** Remove the redundant \"Freeze Physics\" / \"Unfreeze\" button from [`FilterToolbar.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T165618-008-wcap/src/frontend/src/components/FilterToolbar.tsx) and deprecate unused `physicsFrozen` state in [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T165618-008-wcap/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx). The force simulation in [`GraphCanvas.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T165618-008-wcap/src/frontend/src/components/GraphCanvas.tsx) autonomously settles into equilibrium via natural energy decay (`alphaDecay(0.028)`, `velocityDecay(0.4)`).\n2. **Collapsible Blueprint HUD Accordion:** Refactor the static overlay in [`GraphCanvas.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T165618-008-wcap/src/frontend/src/components/GraphCanvas.tsx) into an interactive accordion (`pointerEvents: 'auto'`) supporting Collapsed State (`◈ BLUEPRINT HUD [▼]`, occupying $\u003c180\\text{px} \\times 28\\text{px}$) and Expanded State (`◈ LAG KNOWLEDGE BLUEPRINT 